{"name":"Tank Grey","hex":"#848481","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tank","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closed container for liquids or gases.","An open container or pool for storing water or other liquids."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["This term needs a definition. Please help out and add a definition, then remove the text {{rfdef}}."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tank","blocks":[{"text":"A tank is an armoured fighting vehicle intended as a primary offensive weapon in front-line ground combat. Tank designs are a balance of heavy firepower, strong armour, and battlefield mobility provided by tracks and a powerful engine; their main armament is often mounted within a turret. They are a mainstay of modern 20th and 21st century ground forces and a key part of combined arms combat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Mark_I_series_tank.jpg/330px-Mark_I_series_tank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tank","wikidata":"Q12876"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://